{
  "version": "2026-11-10",
  "purpose": "Shared conformance vectors for the episodic timestamp-group pager. Munnin's business_services/episode_page.py and Hermod's independently housed equivalent must both pass this file verbatim; the two test modules record this file's sha256 so a drifted copy is loud.",
  "contract": [
    "One page unit is a timestamp group: every sub-episode block sharing one H3 timestamp, indivisible, counted once in blocks_returned/blocks_total and once against limit.",
    "A boundary is an H3 heading whose text opens with YYYY-MM-DD HH.MM; the historical [YYYY-MM-DD HH.MM] and HH:MM spellings are equivalent, and a cursor may be written in any of them.",
    "The preamble belongs to the first group. A body with no usable timestamp header is one atomic group. splittable=false bypasses splitting for non-episode records.",
    "cursor resumes at its own group, inclusive. next_cursor is the first group not emitted, verbatim, and null on a final page.",
    "max_body_bytes caps UTF-8 content bytes. The first selected group is emitted whole even when oversized; later groups are added only while they fit.",
    "A read that emits every group from the first returns the stored body byte for byte, even when equal timestamps were non-adjacent."
  ],
